{# _shared/_includes/case/material/material-redact-popover.njk

   Redact popover for the materials viewer's "Redact this document" button
   (see material-redact.js/material-redact-popover.js) — same interaction
   shape as the factual summary's redact popover (dcf-redact-popover), just
   working against a selection made inside the PDF.js iframe rather than
   same-document HTML text. Deliberately outside #material-viewer (see
   material-panel.njk) so material-viewer.js's innerHTML rebuilds never
   wipe it.

   Single document/tab at a time — no cross-document "redact all matching"
   here (that's illustrated in the factual summary version instead), so
   there's no match-count/view-previous/next stepping wired up behind
   "Find matching text": it's present for visual parity with the factual
   summary popover, not functional. #}
<div class="dcf-redact-popover" id="dcf-material-redact-popover" hidden>
  <div class="govuk-form-group govuk-!-margin-bottom-3">
    <label class="govuk-visually-hidden" for="material-popover-tag-select">Redaction type</label>
    <select class="govuk-select" id="material-popover-tag-select" name="tag">
      <option value="">Select a redaction type</option>
      {% for type in redactionTypes %}
        <option value="{{ type.value }}">{{ type.text }}</option>
      {% endfor %}
    </select>
  </div>

  <div id="material-popover-note-group" class="govuk-form-group" hidden>
    <label class="govuk-label" for="material-popover-note">Note</label>
    <textarea class="govuk-textarea" id="material-popover-note" name="note" rows="2"></textarea>
  </div>

  <div class="govuk-button-group">
    <button type="button" class="govuk-button" id="material-popover-redact-button" disabled>Redact this text</button>
    <button type="button" class="govuk-button govuk-button--secondary" id="material-popover-find-matching-button" disabled>Find matching text</button>
  </div>

  <a href="#" class="govuk-link" id="material-popover-cancel-link">Cancel</a>
</div>

{# Sticky action bar — shown once at least one redaction has been made on
   the current document. Remove all/Save all are illustrative only, not
   wired up. Width/position matched to #material-viewer by
   material-redact-popover.js, not fixed here, since the viewer's own
   width varies (full-width toggle, responsive layout). #}
<div class="dcf-material-redact-footer" id="dcf-material-redact-footer" hidden>
  <a href="#" class="govuk-link" id="dcf-material-redact-remove-all">Remove all redactions</a>
  <span class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0" id="dcf-material-redact-count">There is 1 redaction</span>
  <button type="button" class="govuk-button govuk-!-margin-bottom-0" id="dcf-material-redact-save-all">Save all redactions</button>
</div>
